<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6646" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">capnĭas</span></b> , ae,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καπνίας</span>, smoky. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> (Sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶνος</span>.) <i>A kind of wine</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 14, 3,
				4, § 39</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A precious stone of a smoky hue</i>, of several
			varieties. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A kind of jasper</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 37,
				9, 37, § 118</span></i> (called, <i><span class="en">id. 37, 10,
				56, § 151</span></i>, capnitis = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καπνίτης</span>).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A kind of chrysolite;</i> prob. our <i>smoky topaz</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 37, 9, 44, §
		128</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
